# Keep the build context small and never bake local state into the image.
# The Dockerfile COPYs pyproject.toml, src/, alembic/, alembic.ini AND edge/
# (the playbooks + verdicts the insight engine reads), so everything else is
# safe to drop. pyproject has no `readme=`, so README.md (and all docs) are
# NOT needed by the build -- excluded below.
#
# NOTE: `*.md` below is anchored at the context root (dockerignore patterns
# don't cross `/` without `**`), so edge/*.md still reaches the build context.
# Do NOT change it to **/*.md -- that would strip the playbooks from the image.

# virtualenv / VCS / CI
.venv
.git
.gitignore
.github

# tool + build caches
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.cache
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.egg-info
build
dist

# local runtime artifacts (charts, digests, sqlite DBs)
.charts
.digests
*.db
local.db

# tests + scripts are never installed into the image
tests
scripts

# docs / markdown (no readme= in pyproject, so README.md is not a build input)
docs
*.md
